libm — newlib's own math source, linked into the game as library members
=========================================================================

Why this directory exists
-------------------------
Part of the game binary is the SDK's libm.a, linked in by the original
toolchain. Two of its members are built here from the source they were
compiled from, instead of being kept as disassembly: s_isnan.o (isnan,
0x1313C8) and w_sqrt.o (sqrt, 0x131430, plus its 0x10-byte .rodata at
0x13BF28). The SDK's libm.a members were built from the newlib bundled in the
Cygnus EE toolchain tree (every member's .mdebug stabs name
../../../../../src/newlib/libm/math/<m>.c; FACT #9781). The source files are
SunPro fdlibm code under a permissive notice, vendored verbatim under RULING
#9783 because they reproduce the SDK members byte-exact (task #1856).

Nothing in newlib/ is edited. If a file's verbatim source did not compile to
the ROM's bytes, its member would stay INCLUDE_ASM in its game unit; the
source is never changed to make it match.

