Headers NOT taken from newlib, and why
--------------------------------------
fdlibm.h includes <math.h> and <machine/ieeefp.h>, and w_sqrt.c includes
<errno.h>. In the same tree those are newlib/libc/include/math.h (sha1
c66e9246706d882273902bf69de96353a9a2c421), machine/ieeefp.h (cd4145ff9e65cb9a
84793f5bc46ca8ff3efa918a) and errno.h -> sys/errno.h (a772e37c596d446736ab2611
a470ba1281ad7f32 / f0ed505dc5d05841babb0bf98cf8a60abcc11d25), and math.h pulls
in sys/reent.h, _ansi.h and sys/config.h. None of these files carries any
copyright or permission notice of its own (the tree's ee/COPYING.NEWLIB, sha1
29e2fc78466b79e68bf5077d497c130ae93f791e, lists eleven sources' notices and
names no file). They do not meet
RULING #9783's condition 1, so they are NOT vendored; their licensing is the
operator's review (#8304). GCC's ginclude/stddef.h is not needed at all.

Project-written files (NOT newlib source)
-----------------------------------------
- shim/math.h, shim/machine/ieeefp.h, shim/errno.h: written for this project
  as stand-ins for those headers. Each says so in its first line. They declare
  only what s_isnan.c and w_sqrt.c use: the 32-bit integer types and the
  little-endian flag fdlibm.h's word macros need, isnan, matherr, the SVID
  struct exception, DOMAIN, the fdlibm error-mode values behind _LIB_VERSION
  (the const global __fdlib_version), __errno and EDOM. The values are fixed by
  the SDK objects the build reproduces: e.g. EDOM 33 is the constant the SDK's
  w_sqrt.o stores, and a shim with EDOM 34 measured 1 differing image byte.
- PROVENANCE: this file.

How it is built and linked
--------------------------
The two members are rows in going-decompiled/libgcc/MEMBERS (its source
column is relative to that directory; the defines column carries this
directory's include path and newlib's configure.host define for mips64r5900,
-DMALLOC_ALIGNMENT=16). tools/ee/build_libgcc.sh builds every member the
linker script names with the SDK's own compiler, 2.9-ee-991111 cpp.exe +
cc1.exe at -O2 -G0, and archives them into build/<region>/lib/libgcc.a with
the libgcc members; the yaml places them as splat `lib` subsegments:
s_isnan.o .text at 0x1313C8, w_sqrt.o .text at 0x131430 and .rodata at
0x13BF28 (USA). w_sqrt.o's imports resolve to the ROM's own definitions:
isnan from s_isnan.o, dpcmp through symbol_addrs, __fdlib_version to the
rodata word at 0x13BF10 (symbol_addrs), and __ieee754_sqrt (e_sqrt, still
asm: it does not reproduce, FACT #9782), matherr (game C, cod/031380) and
__errno (game C, cod/015180) through going-decompiled/libgcc/LINK_ALIASES.

Checked against the SDK's own libm.a (tools/ee/sdk-lib/libm.a, an identity
oracle only, never linked): with these shims, the .text and .rodata of both
members are sha1-identical to the SDK objects (s_isnan .text d80aa972...,
w_sqrt .text 9f7f2c93..., .rodata d6dd2c88...) and w_sqrt.o's 13 relocations
are the same set. The whole-image check is landing_gate.sh.
